<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: RUGBY UNION-IRELAND'S CLARKE OUT INJURED.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-IRELAND'S CLARKE OUT INJURED.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-01-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hooker Allen Clarke broke a finger in a match on Saturday and will miss Ireland's Five Nations championship game against Wales next weekend.</p>
<p>Clarke, who replaced injured captain Keith Wood in last weekend's defeat by France, fractured the third finger of his left hand in Northampton's 26-17 English Cup win over Coventry and went off in the second half.</p>
<p>He is expected to be out for two weeks.</p>
</text>
